# oracle: fix rigid/small triangle bodies whose centre of mass lies on the y box edge, with fix deform (remap x).
#   Bodies 7 and 10 are bodies 27 and 30 of examples/ASPHERE/tri (tri.srd): their centres of mass sit exactly on
#   ylo, so the last bit of the triangle centroids and masses (atom_vec_tri.cpp data_atom_bonus: the area from the
#   corner points as read, len3 = sqrt of the squared sum) decides whether domain->remap moves them to yhi with image
#   -1, which changes the lever arm of their setup virial (fix_rigid_small.cpp set_v, x unwrapped by xcmimage). fix
#   deform has no setup() in src/fix_deform.cpp at b332f28, so the run setup must not map the atoms to lamda
#   coordinates and back. Measured with native LAMMPS: step-0 c_pf -0.00307532600454042 at both runs' step 0 (the
#   engine gave -0.00204 and -0.00059 when its centroids and masses were an ulp off).
# oracle-inputs: w771tri_edge.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-13
units           lj
atom_style      tri
atom_modify     first big map yes
read_data       w771tri_edge.data
group           big type 1
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check yes
neigh_modify    exclude molecule/intra big
pair_style      tri/lj 3.5
pair_coeff      1 1 0.1 1.0
timestep        0.001
fix             1 big rigid/small molecule
fix             3 all deform 1 x scale 0.8 y scale 0.8 z scale 0.8
compute         pv all pressure NULL virial
compute         pp all pressure NULL pair
compute         pf all pressure NULL fix
compute         xs all reduce sum x y z
thermo_style    custom step pe c_pv c_pp c_pf c_pv[2] c_pf[2] c_pf[4] c_xs[1] c_xs[2] c_xs[3] lx
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             0
run             50
